Vikram and Betal: The Honest King’s Test (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100143

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a king who wanted to find the most honest person in his kingdom,” said Betal.

He announced, “Everyone will receive a seed. Grow it into a plant and bring it back after one month.”

All the people planted their seeds.

After a month, they brought beautiful plants to the king.

But one boy came with an empty pot.

He said, “Your Majesty, I tried my best, but nothing grew.”

The king smiled and said, “You are the most honest person.”

Everyone was surprised.

The king explained, “I gave boiled seeds. They could not grow. Only this boy told the truth.”

Betal then asked, “Vikram, why did the boy win?”

Vikram replied, “Because he chose honesty over showing success.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Honesty is more important than success.
